{"crc":"453eaee2","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that when `Line3D` objects are created with invalid data (like numpy arrays with extra dimensions), they can end up in a state where `_verts3d` is not set, causing an `AttributeError` when trying to draw them.\n\nThe fix should be in the `Line3D.draw()` method in `art3d.py` to handle the case where `_verts3d` might not exist. Let me check the current code and add a guard.\n\n# path: lib/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/art3d.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n=======\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        if not hasattr(self, '_verts3d'):\n            return\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQVJZ0V8DJX6PMVG10VNG3H","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQVJZ0MRNH0B34JETZ05FV2"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786433341.4648802}
{"crc":"069c320f","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:7e1142f6ffc2a0aeedd0b6fe1bbbeb224282da40d7ee735a770a659162395d5f","instance":"01KZQVK20STWPW3M7XQXT0NBJF","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that when `Line3D` objects are created with invalid data (like numpy arrays with extra dimensions), they can end up in a state where `_verts3d` is not set, causing an `AttributeError` when trying to draw them.\n\nThe fix should be in the `Line3D.draw()` method in `art3d.py` to handle the case where `_verts3d` might not exist. Let me check the current code and add a guard.\n\n# path: lib/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/art3d.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n=======\n    @artist.allow_rasterization\n    def draw(self, renderer):\n        if not hasattr(self, '_verts3d'):\n            return\n        xs3d, ys3d, zs3d = self._verts3d\n        xs, ys, zs = proj3d.proj_transform(xs3d, ys3d, zs3d, self.axes.M)\n        self.set_data(xs, ys)\n        super().draw(renderer)\n        self.stale = False\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786433341.465087}
